blurb = "Depicts ox carts passing by a teahouse in Ōtsu (present-day Shiga prefecture). The eponymous well is in the bottom left, so called because of the water that gushed from it. Located on the south-western shore of Lake Biwa, it is the last station on the Tōkaidō before it ends in Kyōto."
